        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "oXE5s",
          "name": "Cover Wrap",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "padding": [
            0,
            120
          ],
          "justifyContent": "center",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "SMSyB",
              "name": "Cover Image",
              "clip": true,
              "width": "fill_container",
              "height": 400,
              "fill": {
                "type": "image",
                "enabled": true,
                "url": "images/generated-1785341788844.png",
                "mode": "fill"
              },
              "cornerRadius": 12,
              "justifyContent": "center",
              "alignItems": "center"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "pFAIB",
          "name": "Article Body",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 28,
          "padding": [
            48,
            360
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "W5Uet",
              "name": "Intro Paragraph",
              "fill": "$text-secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Real-time collaboration is one of those features that seems deceptively simple from the outside. Users type, and everyone sees the changes. But beneath the surface lies a fascinating set of distributed systems challenges that have occupied computer scientists for decades.",
              "lineHeight": 1.8,
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 17,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "fkt6e",
              "name": "H2 Problem",
              "fill": "$text-primary",
              "content": "The Problem with Naive Approaches",
              "fontFamily": "Geist",
              "fontSize": 28,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "X5FfS",
              "name": "P2",
              "fill": "$text-secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "The simplest approach — last-write-wins — breaks down immediately in a collaborative context. When two users edit the same paragraph simultaneously, one person's changes will be silently overwritten. This is not just a bad user experience; it's data loss.",
              "lineHeight": 1.8,
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 17,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "lMlsq",
              "name": "P3",
              "fill": "$text-secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Operational Transform (OT) was the first serious attempt to solve this. Google Docs uses OT, and it works well — but it requires a central server to serialize operations. For our use case, we wanted something that could work peer-to-peer.",
              "lineHeight": 1.8,
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 17,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "ds5OX",
              "name": "Blockquote",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "stroke": "$accent",
              "strokeWidth": {
                "left": 3
              },
              "strokeAlignment": "inner",
              "strokeLinejoin": "round",
              "padding": [
                0,
                0,
                0,
                20
              ],
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "m60d1",
                  "name": "Quote Text",
                  "fill": "$text-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "\"CRDTs guarantee that if two replicas have received the same set of updates — possibly in different orders — they will be in the same state. No coordination required.\"",
                  "lineHeight": 1.8,
                  "fontFamily": "Inter",
                  "fontSize": 17,
                  "fontWeight": "normal",
                  "fontStyle": "italic"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "Xrxhn",
              "name": "H2 CRDT",
              "fill": "$text-primary",
              "content": "Enter CRDTs",
              "fontFamily": "Geist",
              "fontSize": 28,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "dRTMy",
              "name": "P4",
              "fill": "$text-secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Conflict-free Replicated Data Types solve this elegantly. Instead of transforming operations against each other, CRDTs define data structures where all concurrent operations commute — meaning the order doesn't matter. The result is always the same.",
              "lineHeight": 1.8,
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 17,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "wpsOV",
              "name": "Code Block",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "fill": "$bg-card",
              "cornerRadius": 8,
              "stroke": "$border",
              "strokeWidth": 1,
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 2,
              "padding": 24,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "RWjaL",
                  "name": "Code Header",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "padding": [
                    0,
                    0,
                    12,
                    0
                  ],
                  "justifyContent": "space_between",
                  "alignItems": "center",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "XBI3I",
                      "name": "Lang",
                      "fill": "$text-tertiary",
                      "content": "typescript",
                      "fontFamily": "Geist Mono",
                      "fontSize": 11,
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "icon",
                      "id": "a7DHBp",
                      "name": "Copy Icon",
                      "width": 14,
                      "height": 14,
                      "icon": "copy",
                      "library": "lucide",
                      "fill": "$text-tertiary"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "arSOF",
                  "name": "Code Line",
                  "fill": "$accent",
                  "content": "interface CRDT<T> {",
                  "lineHeight": 1.6,
                  "fontFamily": "Geist Mono",
                  "fontSize": 13,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "VBWva",
                  "name": "Code Line",
                  "fill": "$text-secondary",
                  "content": "  state: T;",
                  "lineHeight": 1.6,
                  "fontFamily": "Geist Mono",
                  "fontSize": 13,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "DlowS",
                  "name": "Code Line",
                  "fill": "$text-secondary",
                  "content": "  merge(remote: T): T;",
                  "lineHeight": 1.6,
                  "fontFamily": "Geist Mono",
                  "fontSize": 13,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "g0gqr",
                  "name": "Code Line",
                  "fill": "$text-secondary",
                  "content": "  apply(op: Operation): T;",
                  "lineHeight": 1.6,
                  "fontFamily": "Geist Mono",
                  "fontSize": 13,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "M4x0e3",
                  "name": "Code Line",
                  "fill": "$text-secondary",
                  "content": "}",
                  "lineHeight": 1.6,
                  "fontFamily": "Geist Mono",
                  "fontSize": 13,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "U8grW",
                  "name": "Code Line",
                  "fill": "$text-secondary",
                  "content": " ",
                  "lineHeight": 1.6,
                  "fontFamily": "Geist Mono",
                  "fontSize": 13,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "D0nz4",
                  "name": "Code Line",
                  "fill": "$accent",
                  "content": "class TextCRDT implements CRDT<Doc> {",
                  "lineHeight": 1.6,
                  "fontFamily": "Geist Mono",
                  "fontSize": 13,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "N6EI3s",
                  "name": "Code Line",
                  "fill": "$text-secondary",
                  "content": "  merge(remote: Doc): Doc {",
                  "lineHeight": 1.6,
                  "fontFamily": "Geist Mono",
                  "fontSize": 13,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "i4H44",
                  "name": "Code Line",
                  "fill": "$text-secondary",
                  "content": "    return this.state.integrate(remote);",
                  "lineHeight": 1.6,
                  "fontFamily": "Geist Mono",
                  "fontSize": 13,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "hyvYQ",
                  "name": "Code Line",
                  "fill": "$text-secondary",
                  "content": "  }",
                  "lineHeight": 1.6,
                  "fontFamily": "Geist Mono",
                  "fontSize": 13,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "qyy7X",
                  "name": "Code Line",
                  "fill": "$text-secondary",
                  "content": "}",
                  "lineHeight": 1.6,
                  "fontFamily": "Geist Mono",
                  "fontSize": 13,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "kSASl",
              "name": "H3 Architecture",
              "fill": "$text-primary",
              "content": "Architecture Decisions",
              "fontFamily": "Geist",
              "fontSize": 22,
              "fontWeight": "600"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "tAAdx",
              "name": "P5",
              "fill": "$text-secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "We chose Yjs as our CRDT library for its maturity and performance characteristics. The architecture consists of three layers: a thin client SDK that wraps Yjs, a WebSocket relay server for propagating updates, and an optional persistence layer backed by PostgreSQL.",
              "lineHeight": 1.8,
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 17,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "YTHcD",
              "name": "P6",
              "fill": "$text-secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "The relay server is intentionally stateless — it simply broadcasts updates to all connected clients in a room. This means horizontal scaling is trivial: spin up more relay servers behind a load balancer and use Redis Pub/Sub for cross-server communication.",
              "lineHeight": 1.8,
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 17,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "dRk4U",
              "name": "H3 Results",
              "fill": "$text-primary",
              "content": "Results & Lessons Learned",
              "fontFamily": "Geist",
              "fontSize": 22,
              "fontWeight": "600"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "W6RCx",
              "name": "P7",
              "fill": "$text-secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "After six months in production, the system handles 500+ concurrent editors with sub-50ms sync latency. The key takeaway: CRDTs aren't magic, but they dramatically simplify the mental model. Instead of reasoning about operation ordering, you reason about data structure properties.",
              "lineHeight": 1.8,
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 17,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
