                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "JiWWj",
                      "name": "Post Title",
                      "fill": "$admin-text",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Event Sourcing in Practice: Lessons from Production",
                      "lineHeight": 1.3,
                      "fontFamily": "Geist",
                      "fontSize": 36,
                      "fontWeight": "700"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "OCAs8",
                      "name": "Post Subtitle",
                      "fill": "$admin-text-tertiary",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "A pragmatic guide to implementing event sourcing patterns without the usual pitfalls.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.5,
                      "fontFamily": "Inter",
                      "fontSize": 18,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "rectangle",
                      "id": "UucHR",
                      "name": "Title Divider",
                      "fill": "$admin-border",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "height": 1
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "LC04N",
                      "name": "Body P1",
                      "fill": "$admin-text",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Event sourcing is one of those patterns that sounds simple in theory but gets complicated fast in production. After running an event-sourced system for two years at scale, I want to share the real lessons — not the textbook ones.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.8,
                      "fontFamily": "Inter",
                      "fontSize": 16,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "whF18",
                      "name": "Body H2",
                      "fill": "$admin-text",
                      "content": "Why Event Sourcing?",
                      "fontFamily": "Geist",
                      "fontSize": 24,
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "gF82K",
                      "name": "Body P2",
                      "fill": "$admin-text",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "The traditional approach to data storage — mutating rows in place — works fine until you need to answer questions like \"what did this record look like three weeks ago?\" or \"what sequence of changes led to this state?\" Event sourcing flips the model: instead of storing current state, you store every change as an immutable event.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.8,
                      "fontFamily": "Inter",
                      "fontSize": 16,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
